Third-party software linked, not distributed

FAISS (https://github.com/facebookresearch/faiss), developed and tested
against version 1.15.1, is linked dynamically through its C API (libfaiss_c)
when this package is built with cgo. It is not part of this repository and is
not distributed with it; the machine that builds and runs an application
installs it (see README.md). FAISS is under the MIT License, reproduced below
from its LICENSE file.

FAISS itself links, as built by Homebrew and by the Linux steps in README.md:

- OpenBLAS (https://github.com/OpenMathLib/OpenBLAS), BSD 3-Clause License;
- an OpenMP runtime: LLVM's libomp on macOS (Apache License 2.0 with LLVM
  Exceptions), GCC's libgomp on Linux (GPL 3.0 with the GCC Runtime Library
  Exception).

An application that distributes a binary or an image containing these
libraries carries their notices with it. What is listed here is what was read
when this file was written; it is not legal advice.

